":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T00:28:44-07:00","id":1389583,"title":"","content":"More than half. The original version has seventeen stories.. The Revised edition keeps seven of these and adds a new one. The original edition can be hard to track down for a sensible price, unfortunately. That said, I do think that they kept the best stories for the Revised edition. Some of the missing ones are fun, but none come close to the two Penny Dreadful stories in quality and zest - those two really are special and it's easy to see why Kevin Murphy got the go ahead to write a full novel (it was originally released chapter-by-chapter on the old WW site, iirc). It's a great read. If nothing else, you will come away with a new-found respect and understanding for the Victorian Language of Flowers <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T04:16:14-07:00","id":1389932,"title":"","content":"I still need to read all of the Penny Dreadful book, started it and got distracted and a decade past. :P But the final Novel Ascension was very interesting, they even name Dropped the Yozis... lot of easter eggs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T15:50:22-07:00","id":1390398,"title":"","content":"Well I found a copy of the old version for what I consider a reasonable price. Hopefully, I'm not missing out terribly by not reading the added Revised story.<br /> <br /> Any other recommendations? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T19:57:56-07:00","id":1390446,"title":"","content":"It is not exactly a novel, but I love &quot;The fragile path&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T20:59:29-07:00","id":1390462,"title":"","content":"I always liked Mister Magic. It was first printed in The Quintessential World of Darkness anthology. It is about the awakening and initial trading of a Cult of Ecstasy mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/706-rickayelm","name":"rickayelm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T01:56:21-07:00","id":1390512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alqamar Alaswad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1389081-recommend-mage-novels-to-me?p=1390446#post1390446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is not exactly a novel, but I love &quot;The fragile path&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Fragile Path is really great.<br /> <br /> It's a collection of in-universe documents (testaments, accounts, stories, lyrics etc.) that tell the tale of the First Cabal. I span a whole chronicle off the ideas in it. Great stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T10:06:59-07:00","id":1391503,"title":"","content":"I agree with The Fragile Path, it a very good text, based on the renaissance and the creation of the traditions. However, I do not recommend Time of Judgement, the Ascension final novel for the Mage end times. I did not enjoyed at all and the characters were strange and boring to me, a Wu keng infernalist-transsexual-wicht and a New York city shaman of the trash (his avatar was a golem of cans and newspapers). I also do not recommend Road to Hell, even being the antonomasial lore novel, it is a crossover of high fantasy with plain characters, very bi-dimensional, the kind of villains with evil mustaches...<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24202,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","user":"Justycar","date":". 05-25-2020, 01:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T11:39:08-07:00","id":1391520,"title":"","content":"A novella was unlocked in the Technocracy Reloaded Kickstarter when it hit $162,000. At $167,000 in funding, a second novella will be unlocked.<br /> <br /> About $3000 more to that second novella as of this post. The novella is at any PDF reward level, so that's $30 U.S. pledge to get the novella and Technocracy Reloaded and all the Companion book giving you a lot of Mage story options.<br /> <br /> The Kickstarter finishes on May 28--you can still get it on it or up your pledge.<br /> <br /> The Fragile Path is very interesting and good for giving some history of the Traditions--you have stories and even songs (for Bernadette from the Celestial Chorus).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-27T05:47:16-07:00","id":1391905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1389081-recommend-mage-novels-to-me?p=1389334#post1389334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone read Truth Beyond Paradox?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m a few stories in, not nearly finished. So far it\u2019s pretty trippy, and the authors have done a good job of avoiding game jargon and instead focusing on the subjective experiences of the focus characters, who don\u2019t always have a context for what\u2019s going on. Hell, <i>I </i>don\u2019t always have a context for what\u2019s going on, which is fine because they\u2019re stories first and game-related materials second. We\u2019ll see how the rest of it goes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T15:50:58-08:00","id":1439733,"title":"","content":"I hope it's OK to revive this with a new question.<br /> <br /> I once saw an excerpt from some novel. A Mage, seems to be newly Awakened, hangs himself from Yggdrasil. Some spirit, maybe Ratatosk or a bird, is giving him an overview of the cosmos, Norse-style. Yggdrasil = the whole Tellurian, Mid-Garth = the material world, I think Alfheim and Nidavellir and Svartalfheim are the Dreaming, Nifhlheim = the Underworld, and so on.<br /> <br /> Was this part of a Mage novel? Which one? Is it good?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.